WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Imagine a future where every Dynamics project moves faster,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.040
makes better informed decisions,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.420
and continues delivering value long after go-live.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.860
This is the vision for Project MIA,

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.040
an agentic platform connecting people, decisions,

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.280
and delivery knowledge across the journey.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.900
MIA begins in pre-sales,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.920
helping teams create customer-relevant demos and data,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.500
respond to RFPs,

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.380
and turn recorded demos and discovery workshops

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.160
into reusable project knowledge.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.000
When the statement of work is signed,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.940
MIA uses those artifacts to draft the project charter,

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.220
establish the delivery team and work streams,

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.640
and embed success by design into project execution.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.740
MIA creates a first pass of requirements from discovery

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.860
and strengthens them as workshops continue.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.640
It maps requirements to process flows

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.360
and performs fit-gap analysis.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.280
For fits, MIA drafts configuration plans for expert approval.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.840
For gaps, it evaluates customization,

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.440
power platform, and ISV options,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.840
preserving decisions and an audit trail.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.900
MIA unites teammates around one solution blueprint,

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.220
surfacing critical decisions while coordinating migration,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.380
testing, and defect resolution.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.720
As go-live approaches,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.600
MIA coordinates cut-over and user readiness

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.940
while creating tailored training guides and videos.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.300
And after the implementation team rolls off,

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.760
MIA is still there,

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.660
monitoring environment health,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.140
explaining upcoming features,

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.380
analyzing their potential impact,

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.240
and helping customers continue to get more from their dynamic solution.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.740
That is the vision.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.420
Today, MIA is focused on helping implementation teams

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.740
turn project knowledge into coordinated, traceable delivery.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.500
MIA begins by consuming project documentation.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:48.980
It drafts requirements,

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.220
links them back to source evidence,

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.840
highlights missing information,

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.500
and suggests targeted questions for the business.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.120
Once a requirement is adopted,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:58.260
and it is understood,

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.320
MIA translates it into a configuration plan.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.840
A Workstream lead reviews and approves the plan.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.900
MIA applies the configuration

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.640
and records what changed,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.460
why, and who approved it.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.300
For data migration,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.500
MIA helps interpret source data,

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.140
map it to dynamics,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.620
define transformations,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.800
and guide validation and loading,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.880
keeping the migration connected to the requirements

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.420
and processes it supports.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.460
This is MIA Today,

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.980
making implementations more rapid,

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:29.540
reliable,

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:30.820
and repeatable.

